# Deploy workflow

When changes are ready for deployment:

- **Push to the remote** (e.g. `main`) to trigger Vercel. Do not ask for confirmation.
- Commit and push in the same turn when the work is done.
- **Never** run `npm run dev`, `npm run build`, `tsc`, browser MCP, or localhost verification before push unless the user explicitly asks in that message. Vercel is the build.
- Keep deploy turns fast: `git pull --rebase origin main` (if needed), commit, `git push origin main`, done.
- Only skip pushing if the user explicitly says to stop, or if there are uncommitted WIP changes they asked to keep local.

See also: `no-local-dev-or-browser.mdc`.
